---
// How asset-bearing coins are kept out of an ordinary payment.
// Outpoints and values are invented.
---

<svg
  class="u-dg"
  viewBox="0 0 640 534"
  role="img"
  aria-labelledby="dg-prot-t dg-prot-d"
  xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg"
>
  <title id="dg-prot-t">How asset-bearing coins are kept out of an ordinary payment</title>
  <desc id="dg-prot-d">
    Five coins owned by one wallet enter a classifier. The classifier asks, for
    each coin, whether it carries an inscription, an indexed protocol balance, a
    rare satoshi candidate, or a user lock. Two coins carry nothing and are
    placed in the spendable pool, which is what a plain payment may draw from. Two
    coins carry an artifact or a token balance and are placed in the protected
    pool, drawn with a hatched fill and labelled Protected. A fifth coin could not
    be checked because the rare satoshi service did not answer, and it is placed
    in the protected pool as well, because unknown is treated as unsafe rather
    than as safe. A plain send is drawn taking a single arrow from the spendable
    pool only. Spending a protected coin requires the flow built for that asset
    plus a named confirmation, drawn as a separate path.
  </desc>

  <defs>
    <pattern id="dg-hatch" width="7" height="7" patternTransform="rotate(45)" patternUnits="userSpaceOnUse">
      <rect width="2.2" height="7" class="dg-hatch-fill" />
    </pattern>
  </defs>

  <text class="dg-kicker" x="0" y="14">CLASSIFY BEFORE YOU SELECT</text>

  <!-- Column heads -->
  <text class="dg-h" x="0" y="42">Your coins</text>
  <text class="dg-h" x="228" y="42">Checked</text>
  <text class="dg-h" x="392" y="42">Sorted into two pools</text>

  <!-- Coins -->
  <rect class="dg-panel" x="0.75" y="54.75" width="196.5" height="42.5" rx="3" />
  <text class="dg-mono" x="14" y="74">a1f2...:0</text>
  <text class="dg-sm dg-dim" x="14" y="90">0.01200000 BTC, plain</text>

  <rect class="dg-panel" x="0.75" y="104.75" width="196.5" height="42.5" rx="3" />
  <text class="dg-mono" x="14" y="124">a1f2...:1</text>
  <text class="dg-sm dg-dim" x="14" y="140">0.00330000 BTC, plain</text>

  <rect class="dg-panel" x="0.75" y="154.75" width="196.5" height="42.5" rx="3" />
  <text class="dg-mono" x="14" y="174">7c9b...:0</text>
  <text class="dg-sm dg-dim" x="14" y="190">0.00000546 BTC, inscription</text>

  <rect class="dg-panel" x="0.75" y="204.75" width="196.5" height="42.5" rx="3" />
  <text class="dg-mono" x="14" y="224">be31...:2</text>
  <text class="dg-sm dg-dim" x="14" y="240">0.00000330 BTC, token</text>

  <rect class="dg-panel" x="0.75" y="254.75" width="196.5" height="42.5" rx="3" />
  <text class="dg-mono" x="14" y="274">4d70...:0</text>
  <text class="dg-sm dg-dim" x="14" y="290">0.00051000 BTC, unchecked</text>

  <!-- Classifier -->
  <rect class="dg-panel-2" x="222.75" y="54.75" width="146.5" height="242.5" rx="4" />
  <text class="dg-sm" x="236" y="80">Does this coin carry</text>
  <text class="dg-sm dg-dim" x="236" y="102">an inscription?</text>
  <text class="dg-sm dg-dim" x="236" y="122">a token balance?</text>
  <text class="dg-sm dg-dim" x="236" y="142">a rare-sat candidate?</text>
  <text class="dg-sm dg-dim" x="236" y="162">a lock you set?</text>
  <path class="dg-rule" d="M236 178 L356 178" />
  <text class="dg-sm" x="236" y="200">If a check cannot</text>
  <text class="dg-sm" x="236" y="220">finish, the answer</text>
  <text class="dg-sm" x="236" y="240">is treated as yes.</text>
  <text class="dg-sm dg-dim" x="236" y="272">Unknown is not safe.</text>

  <path class="dg-arrow" d="M198 76 L221 76" />
  <path class="dg-arrow" d="M198 126 L221 126" />
  <path class="dg-arrow" d="M198 176 L221 176" />
  <path class="dg-arrow" d="M198 226 L221 226" />
  <path class="dg-arrow" d="M198 276 L221 276" />

  <!-- Spendable pool -->
  <rect class="dg-panel" x="392.75" y="54.75" width="246.5" height="94.5" rx="4" />
  <text class="dg-h" x="406" y="78">Spendable</text>
  <text class="dg-mono dg-dim" x="406" y="100">a1f2...:0</text>
  <text class="dg-mono dg-dim" x="406" y="120">a1f2...:1</text>
  <text class="dg-sm dg-dim" x="406" y="140">A plain payment may use these.</text>

  <!-- Protected pool -->
  <rect class="dg-hold" x="392.75" y="164.75" width="246.5" height="132.5" rx="4" />
  <rect x="392.75" y="164.75" width="246.5" height="132.5" rx="4" fill="url(#dg-hatch)" opacity="0.16" />
  <text class="dg-h" x="406" y="188">Protected</text>
  <text class="dg-mono dg-dim" x="406" y="210">7c9b...:0</text>
  <text class="dg-mono dg-dim" x="406" y="230">be31...:2</text>
  <text class="dg-mono dg-dim" x="406" y="250">4d70...:0</text>
  <text class="dg-sm dg-dim" x="406" y="272">Never selected to fund a</text>
  <text class="dg-sm dg-dim" x="406" y="288">plain payment.</text>

  <path class="dg-arrow" d="M370 100 L391 100" />
  <path class="dg-arrow" d="M370 230 L391 230" />

  <!-- Outcomes -->
  <rect class="dg-panel" x="0.75" y="326.75" width="310.5" height="98.5" rx="4" />
  <text class="dg-kicker" x="16" y="350">FROM SPENDABLE</text>
  <text class="dg-sm" x="16" y="374">Send 0.005 BTC to a friend.</text>
  <text class="dg-sm dg-dim" x="16" y="396">Nothing is asked about assets, because</text>
  <text class="dg-sm dg-dim" x="16" y="412">no asset can be reached from this pool.</text>

  <rect class="dg-panel" x="328.75" y="326.75" width="310.5" height="98.5" rx="4" />
  <text class="dg-kicker" x="344" y="350">FROM PROTECTED</text>
  <text class="dg-sm" x="344" y="374">Move the inscription itself.</text>
  <text class="dg-sm dg-dim" x="344" y="396">Uses the flow built for that asset, and</text>
  <text class="dg-sm dg-dim" x="344" y="412">asks you to confirm by name first.</text>

  <!-- Closing rule -->
  <rect class="dg-panel-2" x="0.75" y="440.75" width="638.5" height="92.5" rx="4" />
  <text class="dg-kicker" x="16" y="464">WHY THIS EXISTS</text>
  <text class="dg-sm" x="16" y="488">
    An inscription lives inside an ordinary coin. A wallet that treats every coin as plain bitcoin can
  </text>
  <text class="dg-sm" x="16" y="508">
    spend a collectible as pocket change. Holding those coins back is the point, not a bug. Frozen value
  </text>
  <text class="dg-sm" x="16" y="528">still counts in your total balance; it just does not count as available.</text>
</svg>
